      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><strong>Energy sector experience is a local asset.</strong> Houston's dominant industry clusters around energy — upstream, midstream, downstream, and the growing energy transition sector. Candidates with energy sector experience have a home-court advantage that does not exist in any other US market.</li>
        <li><strong>Texas Medical Center creates a parallel economy.</strong> TMC is the largest medical complex in the world — over 60 institutions, 106,000 employees. Healthcare professionals, administrators, researchers, and business operations roles are abundant and well-compensated in Houston regardless of energy market cycles.</li>
        <li><strong>Relationship-driven hiring is the norm.</strong> The Houston business community is tight-knit and relationship-oriented. NAPE, OTC (Offshore Technology Conference), and local alumni networks are where Houston jobs are filled — not primarily through online applications.</li>
        <li><strong>Energy transition is creating new opportunity.</strong> Hydrogen, LNG, carbon capture, and offshore wind development in the Gulf are creating new roles that blend traditional energy expertise with emerging clean energy technology. Candidates who can speak both languages are highly competitive.</li>
